ERROR FUNCTION AND FRESNEL INTEGRALS (301)
7.3.8   S(x)=S_{1}\left(x\sqrt{\frac{\pi}{2}}\right)=S_{2}\left(\frac{\pi}{2}\,x^{2}\right)
7.3.9   C(z)=\frac{1}{2}+f(z)\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{2}\,z^{2}\right)-g(z)\;\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{2}\,z^{2}\right)
7.3.10   S(z)=\frac{1}{2}-f(z)\;\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{2}\,z^{2}\right)-g(z)\;\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{2}\,z^{2}\right)
Series Expansions
7.3.11   C(z)=\sum\limits_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(-1)^{n}(\pi/2)^{2n}}{(2n)!(4n+1)}\,z^{4n+1}\]
7.3.12   C(z)=\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{2}\,z^{2}\right)\sum\limits_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(-1)^{n}\pi^{2n}}{1\cdot3\ldots(4n+1)}\,z^{4n+1}\]
7.3.13   S(z)=\sum\limits_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(-1)^{n}(\pi/2)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!(4n+3)}\,z^{4n+3}\]
7.3.14   S(z)=\sum\limits_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(-1)^{n}(\pi/2)^{2n}}{(2n+1)!(4n+3)}\,z^{4n+3}
