7.3.16   S_{2}(z)=J_{3/2}(z)+J_{7/2}(z)+J_{11/2}(z)+\ldots
For Bessel functions J_{n+1/2}(z) see chapter 10.
Simmetry Relations
7.3.17   C(-z)=-C(z),  S(-z)=-S(z)
7.3.18   C(iz)=iC(z),  S(iz)=-iS(z)
7.3.19   C(z)=C(z),  S(z)=-\overline{S(z)}
Value at Infinity
7.3.20   C(x)=\frac{1}{2},  S(x)=\frac{1}{2} (x\to\infty)
Derivatives
7.3.21  \frac{df(x)}{dx}=-\pi xg(x), \frac{dg(x)}{dx}=\pi xf(x)-1
Relation to Error Function (see 7.1.1, 7.1.3)
7.3.22   C(z)+iS(z)=\frac{1+i}{2}\operatorname{erf}\left[\frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2}\,(1-i)z\right]
=\frac{1+i}{2}\left\{1-e^{\frac{\pi}{2}x^{2}}w\left[\frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2}\,(1+i)z\right]\right\}
7.3.23   g(x)=\mathcal{R}\left\{\frac{1+i}{2}w\left[\frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2}\,(1+i)x\right]\right\}
7.3.24   f(x)=\mathcal{F}\left\{\frac{1+i}{2}w\left[\frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2}\,(1+i)x\right]\right\}
Relation to Confluent Hypergeometric Function (see chapter 13)
7.3.25   C(z)+iS(z)=zM\left(\frac{1}{2},\frac{3}{2};i\frac{\pi}{2}\,z^{2}\right)
=ze^{\frac{\pi}{2}x^{3}}M\left(1,\frac{3}{2}-i\frac{\pi}{2}\,z^{2}\right)
Relation to Spherical Bessel Functions (see chapter 10)
7.3.26   C_{2}(z)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{z}J_{-1}(t)dt,S_{2}(z)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{z}J_{1}(t)dt